ression of hypoxia-inducible factor 1alpha in brain tumors: association with angiogenesis, invasion, and progression</article-title><source>Cancer</source><year>2000</year><volume>88</volume><fpage>2606</fpage><lpage>2618</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Cancer||88|2606||bib54|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10861440</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib55"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Zhong</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>De Marzo</surname><given-names>AM</given-names></name><name><surname>Laughner</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Lim</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Hilton</surname><given-names>DA</given-names></name><name><surname>Zagzag</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Buechler</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Isaacs</surname><given-names>WB</given-names></name><name><surname>Semenza</surname><given-names>GL</given-names></name><name><surname>Simons</surname><given-names>JW</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Overexpression of hypoxia-inducible factor 1alpha in common human cancers and their metastases</article-title><source>Cancer Res</source><year>1999</year><volume>59</volume><fpage>5830</fpage><lpage>5835</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Cancer Res||59|5830||bib55|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10582706</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib56"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Zhong</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Semenza</surname><given-names>GL</given-names></name><name><surname>Simons</surname><given-names>JW</given-names></name><name><surname>De Marzo</surname><given-names>AM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Up-regulation of hypoxia-inducible factor 1alpha is an early event in prostate carcinogenesis</article-title><source>Cancer Detect Prev</source><year>2004</year><volume>28</volume><fpage>88</fpage><lpage>93</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Cancer Detect Prev||28|88||bib56|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15068831</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back><floats-wrap><fig id="fig1"><label>Figure 1</label><caption><p>Photomicrographs of HIF-1<italic>&#x003b1;</italic> immunohistochemistry in the gastric cancer progression sequence showing no staining in normal mucosa (<bold>A</bold>), weak nuclear staining in mucosal cells in <italic>H. pylori</italic> gastritis (<bold>B</bold>), moderate staining in intestinal metaplastia (<bold>C</bold>), distinct nuclear staining in high grade dysplasia (<bold>D</bold>), and strong staining in well (<bold>E</bold>) and poorly (<bold>F</bold>) differentiated intestinal adenocarcinoma (<bold>E</bold>) and revealing moderate HIF-1<italic>&#x003b1;</italic> staining; (<bold>D</bold>) High grade dysplasia showing distinct nuclear HIF-1<italic>&#x003b1;</italic> staining. Well (<bold>E</bold>) and poorly (<bold>F</bold>) differentiated intestinal adenocarcinoma showing distinct strong nuclear HIF-1<italic>&#x003b1;</italic> staining. Photomicrographs of HIF-1<italic>&#x003b1;</italic> immunohistochemistry in resected gastric cancer specimens showing focally positive (<bold>G</bold>) and invasive edge (<bold>H</bold>) patterns of staining.</p></caption><graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" mime-subtype="eps" xlink:href="6603524f1"/></fig><fig id="fig2"><label>Figure 2</label><caption><p>HIF-1<italic>&#x003b1;</italic> expression and patient outcome in patients with non-cardia gastric cancers or gastro-oesophageal junction tumours. Left hand column shows HIF-1<italic>&#x003b1;</italic> negative (score 0) <italic>vs</italic> positive (scores 1/2/3/4) expression (<italic>n</italic>=176). The right hand column shows HIF-1<italic>&#x003b1;</italic> expression pattern categorised as invasive edge, negative or focally positive (<italic>n</italic>=173; 3 tumours with diffuse expression were excluded). Log-rank <italic>P</italic>-values are given.</p></caption><graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" mime-subtype="eps" xlink:href="6603524f2"/></fig><table-wrap id="tbl1" position="float"><label>Table 1</label><caption><p content-type="table-title">HIF-1<italic>&#x003b1;</italic> expression in the gastric cancer progression sequence</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups" border="1" width="85%"><colgroup><col align="left"/><col align="char" char="."/><col align="char" char="."/><col align="center"/><col align="center"/><col align="center"/><col align="center"/><col align="center"/><col align="center"/><col align="center"/></colgroup><thead valign="bottom"><tr><th align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">&#x000a0;</th><th align="char" valign="top" char="." charoff="50">&#x000a0;</th><th colspan="5" align="center" valign="top" char="." charoff="50"><bold>HIF-1<italic>&#x003b1;</italic> density</bold></th><th colspan="3" align="center" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>HIF-1<italic>&#x003b1;</italic> intensity</bold></th></tr><tr><th align="left" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>Biopsy type</bold></th><th align="center" valign="top" char="." charoff="50"><bold><italic>n</italic></bold></th><th align="center" valign="top" char="." charoff="50"><bold>0&#x00025;</bold></th><th align="center" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>&#x0003c;2&#x00025;</bold></th><th align="center" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>2&#x02013;10&#x00025;</bold></th><th align="center" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>11&#x02013;30&#x00025;</bold></th><th align="center" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>&#x0003e;30&#x00025;</bold></th><th align="center" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>Weak</bold></th><th align="center" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>Mod</bold></th><th align="center" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>Strong</bold></th></tr></thead><tbody valign="top"><tr><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">Normal mucosa</td><td align="char" valign="top" ch